UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = 'Overview <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Gain advanced knowledge in migration law and prepare to register as a migration agent with a Graduate Diploma in Migration Law at Victoria University (VU).</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Take advantage of VU’s status as Australia’s leading migration law education provider by studying this practical and engaging course, the longest-running migration law program nationwide.</p><p>If your goal is to become a registered migration agent and work in the migration space as a legal practitioner, HR specialist or government worker, this one-year graduate diploma will equip you with essential knowledge and skills in:</p><ul><li>migration law and policy</li><li>legal research and drafting</li><li>submission writing</li><li>professional and interpersonal communication</li><li>knowledge about the migrant experience and human rights issues.</li></ul><p>Enjoy the flexibility and adaptability of this postgraduate program, designed for working professionals. </p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --><!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>On successful completion of this course, students will be able to: </p><ol><li>Critically analyse, consolidate and synthesise advanced conceptual frameworks and technical knowledge of migration and administrative law, exercising independent judgment in diverse professional and community contexts;</li><li>Interpret, evaluate and integrate provisions of the Migration Act 1958 (Cth), Regulations, and associated legislative instruments within cross-disciplinary contexts to generate and justify innovative solutions to complex, multi-faceted problems while respecting client diversity;</li><li>Formulate, advocate and substantiate legal advice for regulatory decisions through complex assessments and professional documentation including briefs, responses, and visa application options and cancellations, balancing individual interests with public good;</li><li>Demonstrate and uphold ethical and professional standards in migration law practice, both independently and collaboratively, while exercising accountability for decisions and actions;</li><li>Analyse and apply advanced knowledge of merits review, judicial review and ministerial intervention processes for visas; and,</li><li>Critically reflect on personal learning and professional practice to plan, implement and evaluate strategies for ongoing development and effective collaboration within broad parameters.</li></ol><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>You’ll meet the knowledge requirements for registration as a migration agent with the Office of the Migration Agents Registration Authority (OMARA) once you have completed:</p><ul><li>your Graduate Diploma in Migration Law from VU</li><li>the prescribed external capstone exam.</li></ul><p>You must also meet some other requirements, including English language proficiency. Find out more about registration as a migration agent at the <a href="https://www.mara.gov.au/"><!-- -->Office of the Migration Agents Registration Authority<!-- --></a>. </p><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>If you''re a <a href="https://askvu.vu.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2336/~/am-i-considered-a-domestic-or-international-student"><!-- -->domestic student<!-- --></a> or you’re not on a student visa while studying at VU, you can choose to study this course online.</p><p>If you’re a working professional like many of our students, you can fit study alongside other commitments with our flexible options. Choose between:</p><ul><li>weekday evening classes, entirely online (Online Real Time; ORT)</li><li>weekend learning, with a combination of online (Online Real Time; ORT) classes and in-person classes in Melbourne and Sydney.</li></ul><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Benefit from practical, applicable learning that makes VU’s Graduate Diploma in Migration Law renowned.</p><p>You will learn from expert teaching staff who have taught migration law at Victoria University for over 35 years and are leading legal practitioners in this field. They include:</p><ul><li>Law Institute of Victoria and Law Society of New South Wales Accredited Specialists in Immigration Law</li><li>Best Lawyers as published in the Australian Financial Review</li><li>the Australian Migration Legislation Collection and the Australian Immigration Companion</li><li>Former Chair of the Advisory Committee to the Specialisation Board of the Law Institute of Victoria in immigration law for many years</li><li>current member of the Specialisation Board of the Law Institute of Victoria.</li></ul><p>As part of your course, you’ll take part in mock client interviews, helping you to learn the kind of questions you will be asked and the kind of responses you will be required to give as a migration agent once you’re fully qualified.</p><p>You may also choose to complete an optional two-week placement program with migration agencies.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- -->',
