UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = 'Overview <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Achieve your dream of becoming an in-demand IT professional. Our diploma offers a practical, supportive program directly leading into the second year of Bachelor of Information Technology.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Our Diploma of Information Technology has been designed for students taking the first step towards our bachelor degree, and professionals building their current IT knowledge and skills.</p><p>We help you prepare for a degree with targeted support and tuition. We''ll also help you enhance your professional-communication and academic-writing skills.</p><p>You’ll learn up-to-date skills and knowledge for a career in IT, including:</p><ul><li>networking (CISCO)</li><li>designing databases</li><li>writing computer programs in Python</li><li>connecting databases to dynamic websites</li><li>scheduling ICT development using Microsoft Project</li><li>using Linux (<a href="https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/lpic-1-overview"><!-- -->LPI<!-- --></a>).</li></ul><p>If you successfully complete this diploma you will be eligible for a guaranteed place in the second year of the <a href="/courses/bachelor-of-information-technology-nbit"><!-- -->Bachelor of Information Technology<!-- --><!-- --></a>, the <a href="/courses/bachelor-of-cyber-security-nbcs"><!-- -->Bachelor of Cyber Security<!-- --><!-- --></a> or the <a href="/courses/international/bachelor-of-data-science-nbds"><!-- -->Bachelor of Data Science<!-- --><!-- --></a>.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --><!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>On successful completion of this course, students will be able to: </p><ol><li>Apply a broad understanding of fundamental information technology concepts across key areas of programming, networking, web development, operating systems, databases, cybersecurity and data science;</li><li>Analyse real-world information technology problems and implement practical solutions using existing and emerging tools and technologies;</li><li>Communicate and collaborate effectively within diverse teams, applying interpersonal and academic skills to hands-on development practice, and;</li><li>Demonstrate ethical conduct and professional responsibility in Information Technology practice, showing adaptability to emerging technologies, including Artificial Intelligence (AI) and a commitment to ongoing learning.</li></ol><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Our Diploma of Information Technology follows a hybrid learning model and is delivered through a combination of on-campus (in person) 2 days a week and online classes 1 day per week.</p><p>You''ll be able to access resources and complete activities online, prior to attending face-to-face sessions, where your learning will be consolidated.</p><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Our <a href="https://www.vu.edu.au/about-vu/teaching-colleges-schools/college-of-sport-health-engineering/engineering-program/women-in-science-engineering-wise"><!-- -->Women in Science Engineering<!-- --><!-- --></a> program supports our current university students, and inspires women to choose engineering and science careers.</p><p>We run hands-on workshops in science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) disciplines for secondary-school students.</p><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Achieve your full potential with The Learning Hub, which helps you develop your confidence, academic ability, and study skills. </p><p>Benefit from in-person mentoring and study sessions, along with a range of digital learning modules that you can access anytime. </p><p>Get help from our online, 24/7 support service to polish your assignments before you submit, and receive guidance on writing, referencing, maths and more. </p><p><a href="/current-students/advice-support/learning-hub-academic-study-skills"><!-- -->Read more about The Learning Hub<!-- --><!-- --></a></p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- -->',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
