UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = 'Overview <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>Gain the expertise required to manage large-scale building projects with the Master of Construction Management at Victoria University.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>This postgraduate course in construction management will provide you with practical and up-to-date skills to lead construction projects, taking into consideration environmental, social and cultural factors.</p><p>By engaging in detailed case studies and hands-on exercises, you will learn how to plan complex building works and address project risks while effectively managing schedules, costs, and building quality.</p><p>You will also have the opportunity to explore the practical application of emerging technologies such as data analytics, robotics, artificial intelligence (AI) and advanced materials throughout all stages of a project, from planning and surveying to engineering and construction.</p><p>With 600 hours of professional work placement under your belt, you will graduate ready to demonstrate your real-world skills to potential employers and succeed in the workplace.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --><!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- --> <p>On successful completion of this course, students will be able to: </p><ol><li>Contextualise advanced project management knowledge, including established theories and recent advancements, to ensure efficient, sustainable, and high-quality construction project completion;</li><li>Implement construction project management principles and practices in new or complex environments, incorporating innovative solutions and contemporary technologies;</li><li>Interpret international perspectives relevant to the construction management discipline, incorporating global best practices into local contexts to enhance project outcomes;</li><li>Critically assess the sources and validity of information and use standardised processes for information management and storage that align with national codes and relevant standards of practice;</li><li>Plan and execute a research project that demonstrates intellectual independence and contributes to the evidence base within the construction management discipline;</li><li>Advocate for cultural awareness, environmental and social responsibility, integration of First Nations Peoples'' perspectives and respect for diversity in all professional activities; and</li><li>Exemplify professional integrity and leadership by collaborating effectively and ethically within multidisciplinary teams.</li></ol><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>During your industry-targeted Professional Experience Placement unit, you will complete a minimum of 600 hours of work placements. This hands-on industry experience will prepare you for high-level professional roles by exposing you to real-world construction management practices. </p><p>Throughout your placement, you will work under the supervision of a qualified construction manager or equivalent professional. You will encounter various practical challenges and workplace dynamics, which will help you gain a deeper understanding of the professional skills needed in construction management.</p><!-- --> <!-- --> <p>In your second year of study, you’ll conduct research in a specialised area, undertaking a comprehensive study that addresses contemporary issues in construction management. </p><p>Your final thesis will enrich the field with new insights and evidence-based conclusions, demonstrating your abilities for rigorous data analysis.</p> <!-- --> <!-- --> <!-- -->',
